WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.050
- Joining us now is a pair of
boss ladies, identical twins,

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:06.460
Antoinette Clarke and Tricia Clarke-Stone.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:08.126
Give it up for 'em, y'all.

00:00:08.126 --> 00:00:09.530
(applause)

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:11.580
They're authors of a new book called

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.870
Double Down: Bet on Yourself
and Succeed on your Terms.

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:16.660
Welcome ladies, why did
you write this book?

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.280
And I'm so excited about reading it,

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.840
cause I just saw a couple
excerpts and I was like yes.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:22.330
- Awesome.
- Yes.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:25.020
- So, we wrote the book to
really democratize success

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.580
for people that look like us.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.410
If we think about it, women make up

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:30.200
about 50% of the workforce,

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.980
but we're highly underrepresented

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.460
when it comes to executive roles.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:36.470
And then, last year alone,

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:40.770
only 24 Fortune 500 Companies
were led by a female CEO.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.300
That's just absurd to us.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.680
- And 24, what's the total
number, like of Fortune 500?

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.880
- Yeah, Fortune 500, and out of that,

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.410
one was a woman of color.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:52.760
So we wrote this book so
that we become the norm

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:53.593
and not that.

00:00:53.593 --> 00:00:56.394
- Yes, normalize, normalize, I love that.

00:00:56.394 --> 00:00:57.242
I love that.

00:00:57.242 --> 00:00:59.150
So it's very, it's authentic,

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:00.700
and do you wanna talk too,
Antoinette, about what

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:02.560
- She's always hogging the space, Kelly.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.670
- I love it, that's what siblings do.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:05.860
- Let's give her some shine.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:07.250
- You know it's taken us a long time

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:08.750
to get to where we are today,

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:12.670
and our book essentially debunks
a lot of status quo myths,

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:14.620
and we're tryin' to
really push that forward

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:16.650
so women understand that
they need to challenge them

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:17.900
so they can be boss ladies.

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:20.030
You don't need to be
an entrepreneur or CEO

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:22.490
to achieve boss lady
status, we all can do it.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:27.293
- Absolutely, so what're some
myths you bust in the book?

00:01:27.293 --> 00:01:29.060
- So the first is everyone cares

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:30.630
only about how hard you work.

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:33.670
But the truth is, people care
about how smart you work.

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:36.360
It's about achievement verse activity.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.920
So you really wanna
focus on the milestones

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:40.180
and not the time.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:42.550
And the way you do that
is to be strategic,

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:46.370
and really lean into clear
goals and objectives.

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:48.500
- I love that, I'm gonna be so much better

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:49.940
for reading this book, I can't wait.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:50.790
So what's the next one?

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:53.710
- And the second myth is
basically people feel like

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:56.560
they should care only about
how well you do things

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:57.760
that are asked of you,

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.300
but the important thing is doing things

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:00.460
that aren't asked of you,

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:02.240
which sounds a little crazy,

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.050
but you have to go beyond your JD.

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:05.590
So beyond your job description,

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:07.160
and think of the long game.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.560
- Exactly, like look, it might not be

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:09.393
in your job description,

00:02:09.393 --> 00:02:11.090
but this thing the other
day wasn't in mine,

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:13.160
and you just do it cause
it needs to get done.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:16.340
And that's what you want,
you just want it to get done.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:18.192
- And that's what women do.

00:02:18.192 --> 00:02:19.025
- I know!

00:02:19.025 --> 00:02:20.900
- Right, yeah you had to.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:21.733
- Yeah, yes.

00:02:21.733 --> 00:02:24.250
- Your advice though, it
just isn't for working women.

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:26.190
- No.
- It's for all women, right?

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:28.650
Cause every woman doesn't wanna
become a corporate executive

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:31.600
or an entrepreneur, but what
we do want is to be celebrated

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.280
and respected for who we are.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:34.580
- Moms that stay at home?

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:39.559
I mean, I would take any
other job in the world,

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:40.690
like, and I have children,

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:43.500
but it is hard to constantly be just,

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.760
responsible for molding this human 24/7,

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:46.770
and you're just at home, and you can't,

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:48.340
you lose your identity,
there's all so much going on.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:50.410
So I think this book isn't just for people

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:53.080
in any kind of industry,
it's for any person.

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:55.280
Like any woman really
trying to find the best part

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:56.610
of you and be the best
you that you can be.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.840
- Absolutely, it's the
best version of yourself.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:01.090
- Well moms are the CEO's of households.

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:02.277
- Right, right.

00:03:02.277 --> 00:03:03.700
- They're the ultimate boss lady.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.620
- Yes, yes.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:07.959
- I make my husband step up though, y'all,

00:03:07.959 --> 00:03:10.100
I'm like, and luckily I
married a true cowboy,

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.633
he does that on his own, so.

